  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RI Facility II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project entails a loan facility of up to $200 million (the Facility) to support Raiffeisen International Bank-Holding AG (Raiffeisen International or RI), a holding company whose primary shareholder is Raiffeisen Zentralbank &#xd6;sterreich AG (RZB).  Raiffeisen International currently holds controlling stakes in 15 banks and several other finance companies in Central, Eastern and South Eastern Europe, namely in Albania, Belarus, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, Czech Republic, Hungary, Kazakhstan, Kosovo, Poland, Romania, Russia, Serbia and Montenegro, Slovakia, Slovenia and Ukraine.  RIs assets amount to EUR 28.9 billion as of December 31, 2004, with aggregated shareholders equity of EUR 1.84 billion, which due to an initial public offering of its shares in April 2005 increased to EUR 2.39 billion.</narrative>
  </description>
